rlpr 1.30 is now available.  current rlpr users are STRONGLY
recommended to upgrade since older version of rlpr won't work right
with libc 5.4.7.

rlpr uses TCP/IP to send print jobs to lpd servers anywhere on a
network. 

Unlike lpr, it *does not* require that the remote printers be
explicitly known to the machine you wish to print from, (e.g. through
/etc/printcap) and thus is considerably more flexible and requires
less administration.

rlpr can be used anywhere a traditional lpr might be used, and is
backwards compatible with traditional BSD lpr.

The main power gained by rlpr is the power to print remotely *from
anywhere to anywhere* without regard for how the system you wish to
print from was configured.  Most importantly, the rlpr client does NOT
use /etc/printcap (this is done on the server-side), and therefore it
is ideal for printing from machines you do not have root access on.

It can work as a filter just like traditional lpr so that clients
executing on a remote machine like netscape, xemacs, etc, etc can
print to your local machine with little effort.

