A new version of software for MUSTEK Paragon 600/1200 SCSI flatbed
scanners (maybe other scanners also work) is now available.
You can use it under Linux and BSD/OS (BSDI).
It should be no problem to port the software to other systems which
have a generic SCSI driver (e.g. SGI-IRIX).
 
The package includes:
 
        + 'xscan' - a Tcl/Tk user interface
 
        + a program named 'pnmscan' which does the scanning and produces
          ppm-, pgm-, or pbm-images
 
        + some usefull example shell scripts like 'scancopy' (and
scanfax)
          to copy scanner data to a printer
 
        + a BSD/OS generic SCSI kernel driver (only required for BSD/OS)
 
 
For more informations and download:
       
http://www4.informatik.uni-erlangen.de/~aoaugust/mustek/mustek.html
 
For download only: 
        ftp://ftp.informatik.uni-erlangen.de/pub/XCept/paragon_1.3.tgz
 
 
