The Linux User Support Team (LUST for short) needs volunteers!  It's
main objective is to support new/novice users in getting "up to speed"
with their own Linux systems.  To join the LUST, either as a supporter
or as a supportee, see below.

News from the L.U.S.T.:

The mailing list has been moved.  Linux International has volunteered
the use of their majordomo to run the mailing list.  All users have been
removed from the hand-maintained list.  Please join/re-join by sending
e-mail to lust-request@li.org with the word subscribe in the body of the
message.

The webpages have been updated.  WGS has volunteered to host our
webpages but are currently busy with another project.  Until such time
that they (or anyone else willing to host us) (hint! hint!) catch up
with us, the webpages will be hosted from my private directory on my
parent ISP.  Check out the pages at:
	http://www.concentric.net/~joat1/lusthome.html

