========================================================
Copyright 1996 thh-computergraphics. 


 I created a simple tool for programming eproms with the "Quickbyte 2.0"
 prommer. This cheap hardware was sold for Amiga and Atari
 computers in the late 80s and has to be connected via the parallel port.
 It seems to me compatible with the so called "Junior Prommer", a project
 published by the German Amiga magazine "Kickstart" in issue 5/88 and 6/88,
 including schematics. I can't distribute any schematics or hardware.

 My drivers works for x86 linux 2.0.22 and implements reading, comparing
 and programming 2764 - 27512. It includes a simple text based
 menu system and a special kernel module "tio" for reliable timing.

 The software and documentation is written mainly in German. If
 there is demand, I will translate parts of it to English but I am not
 sure if anybody outside the German language area has this specific
 hardware (correct me if I'm wrong!).

 You can get the GPLed C sources and a short documentation from:

