Release "4.3.4" of the Stepstone Objective C compiler is now available
from System Essentials Limited for Linux versions 1.2.13 and higher.

See: http://www.nai.net/~lerman

In addition to porting changes for the OSF/1 version, it incorporates
small enhancements to 4.3.3 including the ability to handle linux
include files with asm and attibute keywords unchanged.

As for all our Unix compilers, the underlying C compiler in the
Objective C compiler chain can be either the native, optimizing C
compiler (cc) or the GNU C compiler (gcc), or any other third-party,
ANSI-C conforming, optimizing C compiler.  (This can be set in the
compiler driver script).

Both Linux and OSF/1 Objective C 4.3.4 releases include:

   * compiler-chain driver script (objcc)
   * executable of the Objective C compiler (objcc.exe)
   * source of the original Objective C runtime library
   * sources of the ICpak101 Objective C foundation classes
   * man pages for both objcc and objcc.exe
   * tutorial program

The list price of these compilers is $799.  The software is licensed
to be used on a single machine.

There are also versions available at an inexpensive $199; for these
versions, we cannot guarantee any form of support.

Ports to other platforms are planned, and depend on market demand.
Please contact us, or visit our web site, for more information,

Ken

