MessageNet Systems is pleased to announce a new release of 
"Silent   
Messenger" version sm03.01.02.

Silent Messenger combines three   
technologies into one product. The 
combination of alphanumeric, digital   
and vibrating pagers with
electronic scrolling message display boards and   
voice/data modems 
allow Silent Messenger to be an effective priority   
messaging 
and visual intercom system.

Silent Messenger allows users to   
compose messages or message templates. 
Message templates allow users to   
provide preformatted messages for
frequently used messages, messages with   
complex information, or when
message content must be closely controlled.   
  
 
To send a preformatted message, for example, the user  first selects   
a
message from a list of messages.  The message is then displayed on   
the
screen and prompts the user to select a person to receive the   
message
from a list of names.  Based on how the user defines the message   
 Silent
Messenger can send the message to a scrolling message display   
board,
display the message on a persons pager or do both. 

Silent   
Messenger addresses many of the deficiencies of present   
paging
software.

   *  Allows persons receiving pages to respond to   
their messages or pages. 
      Silent Messenger, based on the response   
to the message or page can
      trigger the paging of other persons and   
the display of other messages
      on message display boards. These   
automated capabilities of Silent
      Messenger have been generalized.   
Based on an event in the life of a
      page or message such as, sending   
a message, responding to a message,
      expiring a message, etc, Silent   
Messenger can send other pages to any
      combination of persons as   
desired and or send messages to any
      combination of message display   
boards in the enterprise, forward pages
      unforward pages or even   
leave a prerecorded voice message in someones
      Silent Messenger   
voice mail box and page the receiving party to alert
      them of the   
voice message. 

   *  Allows message and page forwarding on a scheduled   
basis.
   
   *  Eliminates the need for users to carry MULTIPLE pagers,   
and
      eliminates the need for people to know someones pager pin and
   
     telephone number in order to page them.

   *  Provides compliance   
with the American with Disabilities Act
      relative to the hearing   
impaired. Silent Messenger has been
      specifically designed to   
function as a Visual Paging system for the
      public message display.   
 

   *  Runs Under NetScape:  
      Silent Messenger can be accessed   
via Netscape.  In other words Silent
      Messenger has a WEB server   
built in as part of the product.  This allows
      organizations to use   
the product as an Intranet application or it can be
      put out side of   
the companies firewall and it can be used as an internet
   
     application. 
 
   *  Procomm and Terminal Support.  
 
      The   
complete functionality of Silent Messenger can be accessed via Wyse
   
     terminals connected to Silent Messenger servers and clients. 
   
     Additionally dial access to the entire application is supported via
   
     Procomm.  
 

Silent Messenger runs under Linux kernel 1.2.13 or   
newer. Silent
Messenger uses multiport RS232 serial cards for connecting   
ZyXEL voice/data
modems, terminals, paging transmitters and scrolling   
electronic message
display boards.

The version of Silent Messenger on   
the internet (http://www.trader.com/
users/5013/3977/smparts.htm) is free   
with the following restrictions:

   Number of pagers supported is 100
   
  Number of ZyXEL voice data modems is 5
