License and installation
- ------------------------
When you obtain the software please read and accept the terms of the
License Agreement.
Please read the installation information contained in the INSTALL file.

Specification (long)
====================
(*) - means a completely new or dramatically improved feature in ver.
3.0

HTML features
- -------------
  * context-sensitive HTML 3.2x extended and HTML 3.2X experimental
modes;
    only tags valid in the current context are available
  * full support for all HTML tags and attributes based on the HTML 3.2
    specification by W3C but modified and extended by us with the widely 
    used extensions (including Frames)
  * support for the full table model as in RFC 1942, but corrected to
    support the current practice (like color cells, width on cells etc.)
  * creation of correct HTML documents (according to the extended DTD's)
  o support for different styles of editing: assistive tagging, cut and
    paste, by hand and parse
  * new, very fast parser (100 times faster on big documents)
  * display of current HTML context
  * commands for finding and selecting the parent and child SGML
elements
  o attribute editors
  * graphical options menus for some attributes, like align
  * command to replace the current container element with another
    one (e.g. H1 with H2)
  * separate target command
  o dialogs for selecting relative and absolute URL's
  o special link dialog allowing creation of hyperlinks and the
    destination anchors in one step
  * auto insert of image width and height (GIF, JPEG & PNG)
  * customizable colors for different HTML tags
  o text to table and to list converters
  o table of contents generator
  o HTML tag flexible report tool
  o ready to use and test Form examples
  * customizable dialog for selecting and customizing of colors
  o spell that skips HTML tags
  o rich set of entities, including Latin 1, Greek and user-defined ones
  * keyboard shortcuts for many HTML tags
  o user definable, mode dependent, key bindings
  * automatic hex-encoding of typed special characters in URL's
  o filters to convert between Latin 1 characters and their
    entities (extendible)
  o support for unlimited number of templates
  * comprehensive context-sensitive, hypertext help with topics
    on a selected tag and edited attribute (version related)
  * on-line hints when importing and correcting legacy HTML documents
  * auto correction of invalid HTML documents
  o preview mode that uses Netscape Navigator, NCSA Mosaic, Arena or
Lynx
    (interprocess communication is used for Netscape and Mosaic)
  * new 10 times faster preview mode for Netscape Navigator

General features
- ----------------
  * international release (versions for 10 languages)
  o modern graphical user interface (GUI)
  o multiple editing windows
  * user customizable pop-up menus for mouse-oriented editing and
    features' quick access
  * user customizable toolbars with fly-by hints for icons
  * nice insensitive icons
  * many keyboard shortcuts
  o split window functionality
  * comprehensive context sensitive and click-on hypertext on-line help
    (now the hyperlinks are in color)
  o multiple undo and redo of edit actions
  o all standard editing features like: text Cut, Copy and Paste,
    bookmarks, pair matching, search and replace, etc.
  o commands to change case of letters, spell and sort
  o formatting commands (move, indent, re-format etc.)
  * auto positioning of dialogs under the pointer (less mouse movements)
  o user customizable filters and commands
  o customization via the standard X11/Motif resources method
  o easy localization to left-to-right languages (8-bit characters)
  * special no HTML mode for quick start-up and plain text editing
    (startup time was reduced by 40% in all modes)

International information
- -------------------------
Localized resource files are available for the following languages:
English (default), Czech, Danish, Dutch, French, German, Polish,
Portuguese, Spanish and Swedish. Commands and messages are localized for
each language but the on-line help is available only in English (U.S.).

