-----BEGIN PGP SIGNED MESSAGE-----


I would like to announce the availability of 
Sybernet shareware for Linux and Apache. 

The Sybernet system is a stand alone cgi damon in the Linux
system which holds a http connection to the Sybase SQL server
on behalf of a web client. you might look on it as a cgi middleware. 
The system also works on a Mac using a WebStar and Solaris 
with Netscape servers. We also tested using CERN on Solaris

It basically removes the requirement for developing
cgi scripts or static html files in order to support 
dynamic html page development.

Unlike static html, the Sybernet system produces all pages from 
sybase stored procedures and does not require cgi files to be 
developed using perl or C and uses no non-standard html tags.

Anyone with stored procedure experience, and modest html knowledge
can develop live dynamic pages on their server.

SRI International developed this in house to replace a mainframe
reporting system and it turned out very well. Therefore we choose to
distribute it as shareware to save other Sybase site's the hassle.

This Linux port was done at the request of Sybase employees, as the
web.sql product from Sybase does not support Linux.

Come and try it out at;

http://linux.sri.com/                 (Apache on linux 486/66 clone)

or

http://spacely.sri.com/netscape.html  (netscape on solaris)

