-----BEGIN PGP SIGNED MESSAGE-----

The response from the first announcement of Vosaic has been enormous
and also uncovered several bugs with reentrancy in the Motif libraries.
Another version of Vosaic has now been released, with the Motif 
widgets replaced by Athena Xaw widgets.  This is more reliable and
shouldn't cause unknown X errors.  It's also much smaller.

Vosaic (Video Mosaic) is available as a Netscape Navigator plugin
for Linux from the Systems Research Group of the University of 
Illinois at Urbana-Champaign and Vosaic Corp.

Vosaic supports real time video over the Internet that is embedded in 
standard Web pages.  The technology allows one to view MPEG video 
at 6 to 10 frames per second over telephone dial up connections at 
28.8 Kbits/s.  Higher bandwidths improve video quality.  There is no
download latency - videos are displayed as the data arrives over the
network.  Get the 1 BETA 12 plugin at:

        http://www.vosaic.com

and check out our Saturday Night Live collection.  As this is a
beta release, we'd appreciate any bug reports.  Please mail them to
bugs@vosaic.com.

Vosaic requires kernel 2.0 and above, as well as XFree86 3.1.2.

Besides Linux, Vosaic clients exist for Win32, MacOS, Sun Solaris and 
SGI IRIX.  Vosaic servers run on Win32, MacOS and all Unixes.  The
Vosaic Media Studio is written in Java and allows one to encode and
prepare movies for presentation in a web site with the Vosaic server.
Please contact info@vosaic.com for more details.

Vosaic uses an adaptive algorithm customized for video that is 
sensitive to bandwidth constraints, bandwidth variability and the 
nature of variable bit rate video encodings.  It adjusts the amount 
of data transmitted between client and server based on measures of 
network congestion and CPU load.  Interested parties can also look 
at this position paper:

        http://choices.cs.uiuc.edu/srg/stan/video.ps

stan

