Anouncing the release of version 0.1 beta of NewsWire
for Linux ELF/X11 systems.

   http://www.cdm.com.mx/newswire

NewsWire is a specialized mini WWW browser that presents 
information in a ticker-tape manner.

Some of NewsWire's characteristics:

  * No special server is required. Any HTTP server can 
    be used to create NewsWire services. 

  * Index documents that point to other NewsWire services
    can be created. 

  * NewsWire documents can be created on the fly with CGI 
    or any other method supported by your server. 

  * Proxy Servers are supported. 

  * Can be configured as a helper application in your browser. 
 
  * Server side control over document refresh time. 

For more information please visit:

    http://www.cdm.com.mx/newswire

To demonstrate the use of NewsWire I have created 
"The Linux News Agency". A service by which anyone can post
a Linux related news item to be immediately relayed to NewsWire
users arround the globe. (Well almost immediately, they are
screened first). Please check:

    http://www.cdm.com.mx/newswire/LinuxNews.html

