I have just made a new release of the e2fsprogs distribution, containing
the filesystem utilities for the EXT2 filesystem.  All users of
e2fsprogs are urged to upgrade to the 1.06 version as soon as possible.
This release fixes a rather serious bug that has been with e2fsck for a
very long time; if the master block group descriptors get corrupted,
e2fsck in preen mode will inadvertently trash all of the backup block
group descriptors as well.  This this can cause severe filesystem
damage.

This release also fixes a number of more minor bugs; see the release
notes below for more details.  

The release can be retrieved from tsx-11.mit.edu, in the standard
location: /pub/linux/packages/ext2fs.

Enjoy!!

