-----BEGIN PGP SIGNED MESSAGE-----

I inquired on usenet recently about the availabilty of this and have got 
no replies so I decided to try and hand patch it into the kernel myself.

This patch adds user ip accounting to the kernel. The programs to control 
it are in the ipacct-0.7a package.
This kernel patch accounts all bytes send or received on the ip level and 
exports this data via the proc filesystem. It also allows the admin to 
control the ip access on a per user basis and also allows certain routes 
to be weighted with different values.

We use the patch here for stopping non-admin users from accessing the 
internet while giving them access to the local network.

It is working perfectly on the skynet.ul.ie server now for a week.

If anyone is interested in getting my diffs for Linux 2.0.21 they are
available on 

   ftp://skynet.ul.ie/pub/linux/kernels/patches/ipacct/linux-2.0.21.patch

The ipacct-0.7a is also available on the above site in

   ftp://skynet.ul.ie/pub/linux/utils/system/ipacct-0.7a.tar.gz

If anyone could point out any problems with just this patch and not the
ipacct user system I would be happy as we need this patch to stop users
using the internet.

