9 October 96 (2100 CST)

Linux Logger Version 0.1a

This is a pre-pre beta version of Linux logger. There are still many
things to be done. As of right now it only supports one contest. (CQ-WW)
This was chosen because that is the next major contest I plan on
operating in.

i have compiled this as a static program. Of course if it doesn't work
let me know, and I will see what the problem is. You shouldn't need any
other libraries than libc. This is an ELF only distribution. I have
chosen to use INT's grid widget in this product. It works rather nicely
I think, and pretties up the display. Right now the logger does NOT send
CW, and makes some stupid assumptions. It assumes that the RS(T) will
always be greater than 40 (the max zone) . Also it assumes the exchange
is in RST zone format. It is still crashing when put in the other way.
It writes a file in a special format, and I am working on the post
contest program to parse this file. Really it is in comma delimited
ascii. I plan on making the "save" menu item save in a non-comma
delimited format.

You can get the latest shareware version from my FTP site
(ftp://ftp.dtx.net/~foggie) you can also get the latest info about it on
my web page at http://www.dtx.net/~foggie

