DISLIN is a high level and easy to use graphics library for
displaying data as curves, bar graphs, pie charts, 3D-colour plots,
surfaces, contours and maps. Version 6.3 of DISLIN is now released.

DISLIN is available for several C and Fortran compilers. It's free
for GCC/DJGPP and GCC/Linux. For Linux, DISLIN supports Fortran
programming with f2c and g77. It uses X11 for graphical screen output
and several formats such as PostScript for file output.

DISLIN is available from the FTP sites

     ftp://ftp.gwdg.de/pub/grafik/dislin     (fast connection)
     ftp://linhmi.mpae.gwdg.de/pub/dislin    (slow connection)

A DISLIN manual in PostScript form is given in the file

     dislin_manual.63.tar.gz


The Linux version of DISLIN for gcc, f2c and g77 can be found in the files

     unix/dislin_linux_1.63.tar.gz  (Part I)
     unix/dislin_linux_2.63.tar.gz  (Part II)

Installation instructions for Linux and UNIX are given in the file

     unix/README.UNX

