Hi,

due to a lot of flames that the program name "mc" is already used
by "Midnight Commander" I want to explain what MacroCALC does during
installation. I know that "Midnight Commander" exists. I use it
myself. MacroCALC was first distributed in 1990 on COHERENT and since
then ported to other Unixes and sold as a shareware product a couple
of hundred times. I could never decide to change the name cause most of
the customers use "mc" in their shell scripts. The installation
script of MacroCALC asks for a seperate directory during installation.
All files are installed in this directory, nothing is overwritten if
this is a new directory. The only file which is installed in "/etc" is
".arxrc" a configuration script which is called in "/etc/profile".
If You don't like the software You can remove the new directory and
the file "/etc/.arxrc" and it's call in "/etc/profile" - that's it.
In "/etc/.arxrc" the directory is added to the PATH and MANPATH
variables AT THE END. If You had installed "Midnight Commander"
or any other program called "mc", the program works the same way
after MacroCALC's installation. In addition the installation script
tells You exactly that. And it tells You that You can call MacroCALC
with the alternate name "321". Also the command "man 321" works.
I hope this is enought explanation. Please no more flames due to the
name, but flame the program - I will try to improve it.

Regards Axel

PS. An "ELF"-version of the software will be available soon.

