pciconf 1.0 is available in:

<ftp://ftp.picturel.com/pub/source/pciconf-1.0.tar.gz>,

or

<http://www.picturel.com>

and follow the links ot the FTP site.

pciconf is a Linux module and a TCL extension that allows processes to
read information from the configuration space of PCI devices. This
allows access to the entire configuration space, so processes can get
at values that are not normally available via /proc/pci, either
because /proc/pci is not as programmer friendly, doesn't display the
number, or the fields are part of device specific extensions to the
configuration space. (This is allowed by the PCI Specification.)

The package also includes a TCL extension that allows TCL scripts
access to the configuration space through the suplied driver.

The driver allows read/write access to the configuration space, so is
useful to device driver writers fiddling with the newly installed
board. The supplied installation restricts write access to root.

I've released this software under GNU Copyleft. Mail me directly with
comments, complaints, or kudos. Enjoy.
