Streaming 'Fast-Start' QuickTime(tm) Conversion
Tool for Unix Webmasters and Multimedia Production 
- ---------------------------------------------------

Digigami is looking for Beta testers for MovieScreamer --
our multi-platform 'Fast-Start' publishing and conversion 
tool for QuickTime(tm) movies.

'Fast-Start' QuickTime movies are standard 'flattened' movie files that
have been 're-organized' for playback over the Internet (or corporate
Intranets).

Every QuickTime movie on the Internet should be converted to
the 'Fast-Start' format.

'Fast-Start' movies allow persons to play QuickTime movies before the
entire movie has downloaded (i.e. streamed playback).  This streamed
playback can be done through Digigami's CineWeb plug-ins for Navigator, 
through Navigator 3.0's native QuickTime plug-ins or anyone's elses
QuickTime plug-in that is 'streaming' enabled.

A 'Fast-Start' QuickTime movie is a non-proprietary format which can be
played back in any standard QuickTime viewer just like regular QuickTime
movies.
########################################################################
Digigami is looking for Unix Webmasters who have existing QuickTime 
movies and want the ability to convert existing and/or new movies 
to the 'Fast-Start' format directly on their Unix web servers.
	
We are currently testing on the following platforms:

