                  WebThreads, LLC of Vienna, VA, USA
 
                         is pleased to announce
 
    WebThreads(tm) 1.0.1 WebSite Interactivity and Visitor Tracking Solution
 
                     ****  Commercial Release  ****
 
            for Linux, Solaris, BSDI, AIX, FreeBSD, and Irix
                     (Windows NT/95 version in BETA)

          available for download at http://www.webthreads.com 
	  
 
 DESCRIPTION:
 
 Webthreads(tm) allows you to create truly INTERACTIVE web sites that
 respond and change in real time to individual visitors based on their
 actions on a web site while providing you, the webmaster, with a tremendous
 amount of information about what those visitors are doing on your site.
 
 Webthreads is a lightweight and easy to install set of CGI scripts
 written entirely in C that greatly enhance the flexibility, interactivity
 and visitor traffic reporting accuracy of standard World Wide Web servers.
 
 Webthreads extends the capabilities of standard World Wide Web servers,
 such as Apache, NCSA, CERN, and Netscape to include:
 
 1. Visit Session Tracking and Reporting (Not Hit Counts!!)
 
    Webthreads creates a unique session, or "thread", for each visitor
    that comes to a site. Every request that the visitor makes to the
    web site is separately recorded and time/date stamped. As a result,
    complete "click trails" are maintained for each visitor no matter what
    browser is used.
 
    These session recordings are then dumped into industry standard
    dBase IV(tm) compatible databases. All of the Webthreads reporting
    functionality is available on-line on your web site behind password
    protected pages. Webthreads provides up to the minute reports on what's 
    being done by your visitor community.
 
    The reports provided include:
 
    a. number of unique visits to the web site over user specified intervals
    b. average number of pages requested per visit
    c. duration of a visit to the site
    d. types of browsers being used
    e. referrer report
    f. detailed visit/session report (lists out the pages a particular visitor
       selected and how long each page was seen).
    g. most popular entry page/most popular exit page
    h. etc.
 
 2. Per Visitor "State"/Interactivity/Dynamic Page Generation
 
    In conjunction with the per visitor tracking, Webthreads maintains a 
    live memory of visitor actions, called the "state", which follows the 
    visitor as he or she travels through the site. 
 
    Webthreads also offers a custom server parsed extension to the HTML
    layout language, which we call Interactive HTML or iHTML. iHTML allows a
    web designer to specify directly within the HTML files themselves how
    those pages should change on the fly based on what the current visitor
    has done on the site. Every form, page, link, imagemap and graphic
    selected during any point in the visitor's session may be used to
    customize the web site for that vistor. As a result, each visitor to 
    your web site will have a unique, personalized web site experience.
 
    For example, Webthreads makes the following kinds of things possible:
 
    a. welcome messages that appear only the first time a visitor calls a 
       specific page.
 
    b. an active table of contents that displays where visitors have yet to
       go based on where they have been on the site.
 
    c. helpful hints that that guide your visitor through your site based on
       where she's been.
 
    The iHTML extension has been kept very simple. Anyone can us it, whether 
    they are HTML designers or high-end programmers. 
 
    The user's browser will never see any of the Webthreads iHTML extensions, 
    in contrast to JavaScript(tm), which can be seen from the browser. All 
    your visitors will ever see is standard HTML: even if the visitor views 
    your document source, the Webthreads iHTML "magic" will remain hidden 
    from view. 
 
 3. Threadware
 
    Webthreads extends the CGI interface to include the ability to
    call specially written CGI scripts directly from within a web page. It
    provides all the constructs necessary to:
 
       1) separate the function of a CGI script from the presentation and
          user interface, allowing programmers to focus on programming and
          designers to focus on the site's look and feel.
 
       2) make custom Threadware applications (Webthreads style CGI scripts). Threadware is completely
          reuseable within a web site and from web site to web site because 
          it allows parameters to be passed from an HTML page to the 
          Threadware application.
 
       3) allow Threadware applications to pass back to Webthreads data that
          can then be :
 
          a) passed to other other Threadware applications either on the
             same page or on subsequent pages on a per-visitor basis.
 
          b) used in iHTML constructs to customize the content and 
             presentation of the web site.
 
       Webthreads solves the problem of passing data from CGI to CGI
       on a per-visitor basis. It also solves the problem of creating
       reuseable web-based applications.
 
    A Perl Threadware library is available for purchasers of Webthreads.
 
    Look for many examples of Webthreads Threadware available on our
    site. Our own custom Threadware applications will soon be available for 
    purchase.
 
 WORKS WITH ANY BROWSER:
 
    WebThreads works with ANY browser. It is NOT Netscape
    specific and does not rely on Netscape Magic Cookies.
 
 WORKS WITH ANY STANDARD SERVER:
 
    WebThreads has been tested with the Apache, NCSA, CERN, Netscape,
    IBM Internet Connection Server, Spinner, and WebSite HTTP servers. It
    should work with any server that correctly implements the CGI 1.0 spec.
 
 DOES NOT REQUIRE ROOT ACCESS:
 
    If you have a virtual web server running at an ISP, you can still use
    WebThreads. It requires only CGI-BIN access to install and run.
 
 EASY TO INSTALL:
 
    The Webthreads installation is completely automated. It consists of
    unpacking the distribution and running "configure". This brands and
    installs the software into your CGI-BIN directory.
 
 NON-INTRUSIVE TEST DRIVE:
 
    Webthreads does not require you to change your web site in any
    way. The software installs into your CGI-BIN directory without making 
    any adjustments to your HTML files. Your existing CGI scripts will run 
    under Webthreads as they did before. You can test drive Webthreads
    yourself before making it available to your outside visitors by simply
    calling it up in your browser with your home page. From that point on,
    every page you view during your visit will be run through Webthreads.
 
 LICENSE:
 
    Webthreads is licensed on a per-site basis. Please refer to our
    web site at http://www.webthreads.com for more information.
 
 AVAILABILITY:
 
    WebThreads 1.0.1 is currently available from our web site at
 
                     http://www.webthreads.com
 
    for a free 30 day evaluation for:
 
       1) Linux 1.2.x and 2.0.x (a.out and elf)
       2) BSDI
       3) AIX
       4) IRIX 5.3
       5) Solaris 2.4/2.5
       6) FreeBSD
       7) Windows NT (in BETA)
       
       HP/UX and DEC Unix coming soon.
       
 VAR RELATIONSHIPS:
 
    Webthreads, LLC is actively looking to establish VAR relationships.
