Troll Tech is proud to announce the Qt GUI programming contest.

			     What is it?

A contest for programmers, writing free GUI software using Qt (a C++
GUI toolkit, see http://www.troll.no/).  Anyone can enter, there is no
fee for entry, and any program can be entered as long as it is written
in C++ and uses Qt.

The winner will be paid US$2000 and two runners-up $500 after the
contest has closed on May 1, 1997 and the jury has done its job.

				 Why?

Troll Tech _sells_ Qt licenses to professional developers, on Windows
95, Windows NT and so far ten UNIX-like operating systems.  Troll Tech
also _gives_ free software developers free licenses for UNIX/X11,
partly as publicity, and partly because we like the UNIX/X11 free
software community.

We wish to encourage more free GUI software for X11 (there isn't very
