root@rymunda:/usr/src/blast,0# tcpblast
give both hostname and block count
usage: tcpblast [options] destination nblocks

tcpblast/udpblast is a simple tool for probing network and estimating its throughoutput
Options:
- -t             use TCP ('t' as first name letter implies it)
- -u             use UDP ('u' as first name letter implies it)
- -p nnn         use port # nnn instead of default 9
- -r             send random data
- -s nnn         block size, default 1024 bytes
- -b nnn         buf size, default -1 bytes
- -V, --version  version
- -h, --help     this help
destination    host name or address
nblocks        number of blocks (0..9999)
tcpblast version: FreeBSD + rzm 960926


WARNING: The throughoutput measurement is very unprecise.

